<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zugdidi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zugdidi is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, the centre of Samegrelo, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enguri">Enguri</a> river and the boundary with Abkhazia. It was the main residence of the Dadiani princes of Mingrelia, whose palace complex is now a museum holding family treasures and relics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> acquired through Princess Salomé Dadiani's marriage to Achille Murat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zugdidi.jpg" alt="Zugdidi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nanika Matua · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E1%B2%93%E1%83%90%E1%83%93%E1%83%98%E1%83%90%E1%83%9C%E1%83%94%E1%83%91%E1%83%98%E1%83%A1_%E1%83%A1%E1%83%90%E1%83%A1%E1%83%90%E1%83%AE%E1%83%9A%E1%83%94_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
